WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.452
Exercise 3: describe your data product.

2
00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:09.953
Orders is one data product. It offers two contract versions as output ports.

3
00:00:10.004 --> 00:00:16.620
The Data Product CLI creates a starter file. Open it in your IDE.

4
00:00:16.670 --> 00:00:26.383
One data product, Orders. ODPS 1.1 adds the type: sourceAligned.

5
00:00:26.433 --> 00:00:34.583
Purpose and limitations: what consumers need to know first.

6
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:48.365
One output port per contract version. The old v1 port is deprecated.

7
00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:53.438
Tags help consumers find the product in a catalog.

8
00:00:53.488 --> 00:01:04.589
Team and support, reused from the contracts.

9
00:01:04.639 --> 00:01:11.704
Validate against the official ODPS JSON schema.

10
00:01:11.754 --> 00:01:21.658
A typo in kind: the CLI names the wrong field and exits with code 1.

11
00:01:21.708 --> 00:01:26.159
Next: a consumer-aligned data product on top of Orders.
